<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henrique of Kongo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1495–c. 1531</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Henrique Kinu a Mvemba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henrique was a son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-kongo">Afonso I of Kongo</a>, educated in Portugal, who in 1518 was made a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> with the approval of Pope Leo X, the first bishop from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sub-saharan-africa">sub-Saharan Africa</a>. He returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a> in 1521 as titular bishop of Utica and auxiliary bishop for the kingdom, but ill health limited his work, and he died around 1531.</p></div>
